.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPADD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm groupadd
.Nd create a new group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl g Ar GID Op Fl o
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl f
.Ar GROUP
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
appends a new entry to
.Pa /etc/group
and (if it exists) a matching locked-password row to
.Pa /etc/gshadow .
With no
.Fl g ,
the next free GID in the user range
.Bq Dv USER_ID_MIN , Dv USER_ID_MAX
.Pq 1000 .. 60000
is auto-assigned; with
.Fl r ,
the system range
.Bq Dv SYSTEM_ID_MIN , Dv SYSTEM_ID_MAX
.Pq 1 .. 999
is used instead.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g Ar GID
Use the supplied numeric group ID.  Refuses to clobber an existing
GID unless
.Fl o
is also given.
.It Fl o
With
.Fl g ,
allow non-unique GIDs.
.It Fl r
Allocate from the system range when auto-assigning.
.It Fl f
Exit 0 instead of failing if
.Ar GROUP
already exists.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
Bad usage.
.It 3
Invalid argument value.
.It 4
GID already in use (without
.Fl o ) .
.It 9
Group name already in use (without
.Fl f ) .
.It 10
Failed to update
.Pa /etc/group .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getgrent 3 ,
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr gshadow 5 ,
.Xr groupdel 8 ,
.Xr groupmod 8 ,
.Xr useradd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
